{
  "id": null,
  "uid": "cowrie-human-hunt",
  "title": "Cowrie Honeypot — Human Hunt",
  "description": "Surfaces sessions that look like a person at a keyboard, not a scripted scanner, so real attacks don't get lost in bot noise.",
  "tags": [
    "cowrie",
    "honeypot",
    "human"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-7d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "How to use this dashboard",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Scripted bots (Mirai/Gafgyt-style scanners, which make up the vast majority of traffic on any public SSH/Telnet honeypot) almost always do the same thing: connect, run the same 3-6 fingerprinting commands in well under a second, and disconnect. A real person behind a keyboard looks different -- typing has human latency, sessions run longer, and the commands vary because they're actually looking around.\n\n**None of the signals below prove a human was involved -- they just tell you where to look first.** A slow network can inflate duration, and some bot families do run more than one command. Always confirm by opening the session in the [session viewer](../../webui/) and watching the actual replay before drawing conclusions.\n\n- **Duration** -- typical bot sessions are under 5 seconds. Anything over ~20-30s is worth a look.\n- **Distinct commands** -- bots repeat the same handful of commands (often just 1-4, always the same ones). Sessions with many *different* commands suggest someone exploring rather than running a fixed script.\n\nDefault time range here is 7 days (real human intrusion attempts are much rarer than bot scans -- a 24h window may simply have none)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Candidates",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Longest sessions",
      "description": "Sorted by session duration, descending. Bot sessions almost never make it past a few seconds.",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "left"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Value"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Duration (s)"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "right"
              },
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "s"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "src_ip"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Source IP"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            },
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Value",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(50, sum by (session, src_ip) (sum_over_time({job=\"cowrie\"} | json | eventid=\"cowrie.session.closed\" | unwrap duration [$__range])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "queryType": "instant",
          "format": "table"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Most exploratory sessions (distinct commands)",
      "description": "Number of DIFFERENT commands run per session, not total commands. Bots repeat the same fixed sequence; a high distinct count means someone was actually looking around.",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "left"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Value"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Distinct commands"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "right"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "src_ip"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Source IP"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            },
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Value",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(50, count by (session, src_ip) (sum by (session, src_ip, input) (count_over_time({job=\"cowrie\"} | json | eventid=\"cowrie.command.input\" | input != \"\" [$__range]))))",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "queryType": "instant",
          "format": "table"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "title": "Combined profile (experimental)",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Session profiler -- duration + distinct commands side by side",
      "description": "Joins the two tables above by session ID. This relies on Grafana's outer-join transform and hasn't been screenshot-verified across Grafana versions -- if the columns look wrong or duplicated, open this panel's edit view and check the 'Outer join' transformation; the two simple tables above are the reliable fallback.",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "left"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Value #A"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Duration (s)"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "right"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Value #B"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Distinct commands"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "right"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "src_ip"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Source IP"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "joinByField",
          "options": {
            "byField": "session",
            "mode": "outer"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Time 1": true,
              "Time 2": true
            },
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Distinct commands",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(50, sum by (session, src_ip) (sum_over_time({job=\"cowrie\"} | json | eventid=\"cowrie.session.closed\" | unwrap duration [$__range])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "queryType": "instant",
          "format": "table"
        },
        {
          "expr": "topk(50, count by (session, src_ip) (sum by (session, src_ip, input) (count_over_time({job=\"cowrie\"} | json | eventid=\"cowrie.command.input\" | input != \"\" [$__range]))))",
          "refId": "B",
          "instant": true,
          "queryType": "instant",
          "format": "table"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "title": "Study a candidate",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Next step",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Found a session ID worth checking above? Open the session viewer (`SESSION_VIEWER_PORT`, default 8080) and find that session in the list, or search this session ID directly in Explore: `{job=\"cowrie\"} | json | session=\"<id>\"` to read every event in order."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "All commands for the selected time range (longest sessions first is above -- use this to read a session's full command flow)",
      "type": "logs",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 35
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "sortOrder": "Ascending",
        "wrapLogMessage": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "{job=\"cowrie\"} | json | eventid=\"cowrie.command.input\" | line_format \"[{{.session}}] {{.src_ip}} > {{.input}}\"",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
